from pathlib import Path
import json
from html import escape
root=Path('qa-artifacts/pre-app-release')
web=json.loads((root/'web-screens.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
flows=json.loads((root/'flows.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
ios=json.loads(Path('qa-artifacts/ios-app/verification.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
ios_screens=json.loads((root/'ios-regression/web-screens.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
ios_flows=json.loads((root/'ios-regression/flows.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
security=json.loads((root/'runtime-audit.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
sync=json.loads((root/'bundle-sync.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
size=json.loads((root/'bundle-size.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
assert len(web)==74 and all(r['passed'] for r in web)
assert len(flows)==19 and all(r['passed'] for r in flows)
assert len(ios)==51 and all(r['passed'] for r in ios)
assert len(ios_screens)==3 and all(r['passed'] for r in ios_screens)
assert len(ios_flows)==10 and all(r['passed'] for r in ios_flows)
assert security['metadata']['vulnerabilities']['total']==0
assert sync['passed'] and sync['iosBundleMatches']
desktop={r['key']:r for r in web if r['profile']=='desktop'}
cards=''.join(f'''<article><a href="{escape(r['file'])}"><img loading="lazy" src="{escape(r['file'])}" alt="{escape(key.replace('_',' '))}"></a><h3>{escape(key.replace('_',' ').title())}</h3><p><a href="{escape(r['file'])}">Production desktop</a> · <a href="web-phone-{escape(key)}.png">Production landscape</a> · <a href="../ios-app/{escape(key)}-844.png">iOS bundle preview</a></p></article>''' for key,r in desktop.items())
flowtable=''.join(f'<tr><td>{escape(r["profile"])}</td><td>{escape(r["name"].replace("-"," "))}</td><td>Pass</td></tr>' for r in flows)
html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Final QA before app versions</title><style>body{{margin:0;background:#071d27;color:#edf5ef;font:17px/1.6 system-ui}}main{{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:32px}}h1{{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,52px);line-height:1.1}}h2{{margin-top:40px}}p{{max-width:90ch}}a{{color:#ffdb8b}}.grid{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(330px,1fr));gap:24px}}img{{width:100%;border-radius:12px}}article p{{margin:0}}h3{{font-size:19px;margin:8px 0}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}}td,th{{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #31505b;text-align:left}}.pass{{color:#9ee2bd}}code{{font-size:14px}}</style><main>
<p>SATs Legends · 20 October 2026</p><h1>Final QA before Android and iOS versions</h1><p class="pass"><strong>Verdict: ready to use as the shared base for app-version development.</strong></p><p>No reproducible blocker remained in the checks below. This is a production-bundle verification, not App Store or Play Store release certification. No Android application has been created in this repository yet.</p>
<h2>Fresh verification</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>TypeScript, production website build, iOS bundle build</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><td>All 37 games, production desktop and landscape phone</td><td>74 captures passed: layout, model containment, clickable controls, assets and runtime errors</td></tr><tr><td>iOS bundle in Chromium, 844×390 / 667×375 / 932×430</td><td>49 captures passed; all 37 games at 844×390, six layout-sensitive games at each other size</td></tr><tr><td>Native app-state bridge stand-in and simulated safe areas</td><td>2 checks passed; background/resume and 47px camera-cutout clearance</td></tr><tr><td>Production gameplay flows</td><td>19 passed</td></tr><tr><td>iOS sync and copied bundle</td><td>{sync['files']} files match the current build byte for byte</td></tr><tr><td>Content and marking</td><td>600 paper variants, 70 challenge prompts and 12 independent data puzzles passed</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Production interaction checks</h2><p>These run against compiled website assets, with production timing enabled. They exercise real clock controls and answer feedback, Help and working-board pause/resume, portrait rotation pause, mute persistence, three-strike racing failure and retry, scrolling race movement and progress, and saving/reloading/reviewing all three mock papers. Production recording playback was observed on desktop and landscape Chromium.</p><p>The rebuilt iOS bundle also passed three focused Core screen captures and ten landscape gameplay flows, including all three corrected reviews. Together with the 19 website flows below, that is 29 successful interaction checks. <a href="ios-regression/flows.json">Updated iOS-bundle flows</a> · <a href="ios-regression/review-phone-mirror_gate.png">Updated iOS review</a>. The runtime dependency audit reported zero known vulnerabilities using the system certificate trust store.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Profile</th><th>Flow</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{flowtable}</tbody></table>
<h2>What changed in this pass</h2><p>The production pass caught a companion character covering mock-paper review text and links. <code>src/components/game-ui/core-paper-presentation.css</code> now hides that companion during review. All three paper reviews were rechecked on desktop and landscape, including expanding a saved answer after reload. <a href="review-desktop-crystal_core.png">Desktop review</a> · <a href="review-phone-matrix_match.png">Landscape review</a>.</p><p>The copied iOS web bundle was refreshed through the existing Capacitor sync command. No gameplay rules or question content changed. Added QA files: <code>scripts/verify-pre-app-release.mjs</code> and <code>scripts/build-pre-app-release-report.py</code>. Generated evidence is in <code>qa-artifacts/pre-app-release/</code>; the existing iOS-preview evidence was refreshed in <code>qa-artifacts/ios-app/</code>.</p>
<h2>Work belonging to the app versions</h2><ul><li>Android: add the native project and build configuration; no APK or AAB is claimed by this QA pass.</li><li>iOS: compile and sign the Xcode project on a Mac, then test an installed build. Chromium previews and a bridge stand-in do not validate native plugin binaries.</li><li>On real devices: check audio balance and silent-mode behaviour, interruptions, physical safe areas, memory/performance, login/recovery and app return paths.</li><li>Replace the existing placeholder app icon and launch screen as part of app packaging.</li><li>The current iOS web bundle is {size['MiB']} MiB uncompressed. Measure installation/download size and memory on the native builds before release; the approved artwork has been preserved.</li></ul>
<p>Both builds retain Vite’s large-chunk warning. The previous <a href="../final-audio-qa/index.html">sound QA report</a> contains per-game cue previews and 46 successful audio scenarios. Its nine Windows WebKit audio checks remain unavailable because that runner has no Web Audio API. A real iPhone audio pass is still required. Previous geometry checks are not being presented as new native-device evidence.</p>
<h2>Production screenshots</h2><div class="grid">{cards}</div><h2>Evidence and assumptions</h2><p><a href="web-screens.json">Production screen results</a> · <a href="flows.json">Gameplay flows</a> · <a href="../ios-app/verification.json">iOS preview results</a> · <a href="bundle-sync.json">Bundle parity</a> · <a href="bundle-size.json">Bundle size</a></p><p>All account requests used isolated QA fixtures; this did not exercise a real family account or live progress write. The pass covers opening/highest-tier production screens and the listed flows, not every random question or complete playthrough. Assumption: verify the shared game and existing iOS foundation before starting separate app versions; store packaging and submission are outside this pass. No external legacy assumptions were used.</p></main></html>'''
(root/'index.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built pre-app report: 74 production screens, 51 iOS-preview checks, 19 gameplay flows')
